# Client UI components (required)

Read `AGENTS.md` for full instructions.

## Arrow functions

Use arrow functions for components and helpers — `export const MyPage = () => { … }`, not `export function MyPage()`. See `AGENTS.md` → Code style.

## Reuse before creating

Check `client/src/components/ui/` first. Reuse `Button`, `Input`, `PasswordInput`, `FormField`, `FormActions`, `Modal`, `FormModal`, `Table`, `Tabs`, `PageContainer`, `PageHeader`, `Dropdown`, and `Spinner`. Create a new file in that folder only when no existing component fits.

## Page file organization

Keep page entry files thin. Structure:

- `client/src/pages/<feature>/<Feature>Page.tsx` — route entry: guards, queries/mutations, state, composition
- `client/src/pages/<feature>/components/` — tables, filters, forms, modals, sections for that page
- `client/src/pages/<feature>/utils.ts` — optional page-local pure helpers

Extract UI into `components/` as the page grows. Reuse across features → `client/src/components/`. See `employees/EmployeesPage` and `registrations/RegistrationsPage` for reference.

## Page layout

New dashboard pages must match existing screens (`employees/EmployeesPage`, `registrations/RegistrationsPage`):

- `PageContainer` → `PageHeader` (label, title, description, action button) → content
- Data lists: `Table` with `loading` / `emptyMessage` (center-aligned by default; use `align` prop to override)
- Create/edit: `FormModal` + `FormField`
- Related list views: `Tabs` with a separate `Table` per tab

## Table alignment

- Default: **center** for headers and cells
- Table-level: `<Table align="left" … />` sets default for all columns
- Column-level: `{ align: 'right' }` on a column overrides the table default
- Flex content in cells: use matching `justify-center` / `justify-start` / `justify-end` on inner flex wrappers

## Loading states

- `Button`: always pass `loading` + `loadingText` during async actions
- `Table`: use `loading` prop for list fetch states
- Never show a clickable submit button without a spinner while saving

## Save button activation

| Form type | Submit enabled when |
|-----------|---------------------|
| **Create** | All required fields filled (`areRequiredFieldsFilled`) |
| **Edit** | At least one field changed vs original (`hasFormChanges`) |

Use `submitDisabled` on `FormActions` / `FormModal`, or `disabled` on `Button`.

Helpers live in `client/src/utils/form.ts`: `areRequiredFieldsFilled`, `hasFormChanges`, `pickChangedFields`.

## Partial updates (DB)

- **Client:** PATCH/send only changed fields via `pickChangedFields`
- **Server:** Apply only fields present in the request body

## Password inputs

Use `PasswordInput` (show/hide toggle). Do not use raw `Input type="password"`.

## Icons

Use `react-icons/hi2` with colorful Tailwind classes on buttons, dropdown items, and actions.

## Form field icons (required)

Pass `icon` to every `Input` and `PasswordInput` in forms (`h-5 w-5 text-brand-600`):

- Company → `HiBuildingOffice2`
- Name → `HiUser`
- Email → `HiEnvelope`
- Password → `HiLockClosed`
- Search → `HiMagnifyingGlass`

See `login/LoginPage` and `register/RegisterPage` for reference.
